      "explanation": "Nitration takes place in presence of concentrated\nHNO<sub>3</sub> + concentrated H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>.\n<br><br>In strongly acidic nitration medium, the amine is converted into anilinium ion (– NH<sub>3</sub><sup>+</sup> ); substitution is\nthus controlled not by – NH<sub>2</sub> group but by – NH<sub>3</sub><sup>+</sup> group which, because of its positive charge,\ndirects the entering group to the meta-position instead of ortho and para.\n<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7kejek2vdnzd6/15117fff-3c91-40a0-8c9e-3146a2c42090/00d0c2a0-0508-11ea-a7bc-b7b08ce8d541/file-7kejek2vdnzd7-320w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2017 (Offline) Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 240 English Explanation\">"
